# apps/proxy environment variables
#
# See /docs/SECRETS.md at the repo root for the full cross-service
# convention (where each value is stored, how to rotate it). This file
# only lists what apps/proxy itself reads.
#
# Real values are never set here or in any .env file committed to the
# repo — only in Railway: each service's Variables tab, set separately
# for the staging and production environments. For local dev, copy this
# file to .env (gitignored) and fill it in.

# --- Server (issue 1.3) ---
# Port/host the proxy listens on. Railway injects PORT automatically in
# staging/production — these defaults are for local dev only.
PORT=8787
HOST=0.0.0.0

# --- Supabase (Epic 5/6 — event writes + API-key auth) ---
# Service role key: bypasses Row-Level Security, required for the
# ingestion path to write LLMCallEvent rows across any project/org, and
# (as of issue 6.2) for the auth middleware to look up api_keys rows —
# RLS grants authenticated/anon no column access to hashed_key at all,
# so only service_role can verify a presented key.
# NEVER expose this to a browser context or log it. Required to start
# apps/proxy at all as of issue 6.2 (src/index.ts constructs the real
# client eagerly and throws at startup if unset) — previously optional
# for local dev since only the *.live.test.ts suites needed it.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# Only needed to run write-llm-call-event.live.test.ts by hand — set to
# a real seeded Project id (e.g. one of the RLS test projects in
# docs/RLS.md) you're comfortable writing a disposable test row into.
TEST_PROJECT_ID=

# --- Queue (Epic 7) ---
# Issue 7.1 judgment call (superseding this section's original
# Upstash-shaped placeholder from issue 1.9): the ingestion queue lives
# in the same Supabase project as everything else, via the pgmq
# extension (`pgmq.q_ingestion_events` / `pgmq.a_ingestion_events`,
# provisioned in supabase/migrations/20260902071700_ingestion_queue_pgmq.sql).
# No new env vars -- it's reached through the exact same
# SUPABASE_URL/SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY client above. See that
# migration's header comment for the full reasoning (avoids a second
# external vendor/account for a non-technical founder; PRD NFR §10.4
# explicitly allows "Supabase-native queuing" as an equal alternative
# to Upstash Redis/QStash). Not yet wired into apps/proxy's own code as
# of this issue -- issue 7.2 changes POST /v1/events to enqueue here
# instead of writing directly.

# --- Observability (Epic 19.2/19.3) ---
# Not yet wired in code as of issue 1.9.
SENTRY_DSN=
AXIOM_TOKEN=

# --- Narration layer (Epic 18) ---
# Which service ends up owning the Claude call (this one vs the
# dashboard) is an open architectural question for Epic 18 — listed here
# as the most likely home given the proxy already holds other
# server-only credentials. Not yet wired in code as of issue 1.9.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
